0</span><span mathquill-command-id=\\"39\\">.</span><span mathquill-command-id=\\"40\\">2</span><span mathquill-command-id=\\"41\\">8</span></span><span class=\\"mq-scaled mq-paren\\" style=\\"transform: scale(1, 1.2);\\">)</span></span><span class=\\"mq-supsub mq-non-leaf mq-sup-only\\" mathquill-command-id=\\"23\\"><span class=\\"mq-sup\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"24\\"><span class=\\"mq-fraction mq-non-leaf\\" mathquill-command-id=\\"28\\"><span class=\\"mq-numerator\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"29\\"><var mathquill-command-id=\\"34\\">x</var></span><span class=\\"mq-denominator\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"30\\"><span mathquill-command-id=\\"32\\">1</span><span mathquill-command-id=\\"33\\">2</span></span><span style=\\"display:inline-block;width:0\\">​</span></span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;<br>The function f gives the value, in dollars, of a certain piece of equipment after x months of use. If the value of the equipment decreases each year by p% of its value&nbsp;<br>the preceding year, what is the value of p?</span></span><br>","question":"","options":[{"name":"A","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">2</span></span><br>"},{"name":"B","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">10</span></span><br>"},{"name":"C","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">28</span></span><br>"},{"name":"D","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">72</span></span><br>"}],"correct":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">72</span></span><br>","solution":""},{"type":"choice","article":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">An equilateral triangle has a height of </span></span><span class=\\"mq-math-mode\\" latex-data=\\"49\\\\sqrt